<title>UK: U.K. Coryton cracker back after delayed restart.</title>
<headline>U.K. Coryton cracker back after delayed restart.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The catalytic cracker at the BP /Mobil U.K. Coryton refinery has resumed operations after a delayed restart, a BP spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;As we were restreaming the cracker, we discovered one or two minor technical problems that needed to be addressed,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>The 60,000 barrels per day (bpd) cracker has now fully resumed operations, he added.</p>
<p>The Coryton refinery has a crude distillation capacity of 180,000 bpd.</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 542 4984</p>
